error[E1014]: `self.x` is `read` for the whole call, so it cannot be assigned through
 --> mem:///main.lu:4:9
  |
3 |     fn peek(self) -> int {
  |             ---- `self` is declared without a mode — that spells `read`, immutable for the call
4 |         self.x = 9
  |         ^^^^^^ write through a `read` parameter
  |
  = note: a `read` parameter is the caller's value, lent immutably [mem.tier0.mode.read]. Declare
    it `mut` if this function's purpose is to change it (call sites then spell the
    mutation), `take` it if the function consumes it, or mutate this function's own `copy`.
